  "slug": "spc-preliminary-filtered-tornado-report-counts-for-dc8be9ce",
  "query": "SPC preliminary filtered tornado report counts for July 1 through July 9 in recent years (2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025). I need the daily or summed number of filtered tornado local storm reports (LSR) from NOAA Storm Prediction Center daily storm reports pages (spc.noaa.gov/climo/reports) for the first 9 days of July each year. Provide per-year totals for July 1-9 if possible.",
  "answer": "I've completed the research. Here's a summary of the findings:\n\n## SPC Preliminary Filtered Tornado Reports — July 1–9 Totals\n\n| Year | Jul 1–9 Total |\n|------|:-------------:|\n| 2021 | **31** |\n| 2022 | **22** |\n| 2023 | **23** |\n| 2024 | **105** |\n| 2025 | **25** |\n\n**Per-day breakdown:**\n\n| Date | 2021 | 2022 | 2023 | 2024 | 2025 |\n|------|:----:|:----:|:----:|:----:|:----:|\n| Jul 1 | 5 | 0 | 2 | 7 | 3 |\n| Jul 2 | 0 | 0 | 11 | 3 | 0 |\n| Jul 3 | 3 | 1 | 1 | 3 | 1 |\n| Jul 4 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 7 | 0 |\n| Jul 5 | 0 | 9 | 0 | 3 | 2 |\n| Jul 6 | 3 | 11 | 4 | 8 | 8 |\n| Jul 7 | 10 | 0 | 2 | 4 | 11 |\n| Jul 8 | 9 | 1 | 2 | **58** | 0 |\n| Jul 9 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 12 | 0 |\n\n**Key takeaways:**\n- **2024 is a massive outlier (105)** — driven almost entirely by the July 8–9 tornado outbreak from the remnants of Tropical Storm/Hurricane Beryl (58 reports on July 8 alone).\n- The other four years cluster tightly at **22–31 reports** (average ~25 when excluding 2024).\n- Data pulled directly from SPC's filtered tornado CSVs at `spc.noaa.gov/climo/reports/`. I enumerated actual CSV rows to get exact counts, correcting several automated miscounts — most notably confirming July 8, 2024 = 58 (not the 60/70 the automated parser initially guessed).\n\n**Important caveat:** These are SPC *preliminary filtered* LSR counts, not final NCEI Storm Data verified tornado tallies, which typically differ after survey review and de-duplication.",
